From: arch-port
Subject: [PATCH] xwayland: 20:9 modes in the emulated mode list

Phones are 20:9 (2400x1080, 1600x720 ...). The emulated XRandR modes
were 4:3, 16:10 and 16:9 only, so a game asked for a lower resolution got
the wrong shape (black bars). Wine / Proton add the host modes to its
own list, so the same modes reach Windows games too.
---
--- a/hw/xwayland/xwayland-output.c
+++ b/hw/xwayland/xwayland-output.c
@@ -339,6 +339,20 @@
     {  864,  486 },
     {  720,  400 },
     {  640,  350 },
+    /* 20:9 (2.22): phone screens (2400x1080, 1600x720); games that pick a
+     * lower resolution keep the screen's shape instead of black bars */
+    { 3200, 1440 },
+    { 2400, 1080 },
+    { 2160,  972 },
+    { 2000,  900 },
+    { 1920,  864 },
+    { 1800,  810 },
+    { 1600,  720 },
+    { 1440,  648 },
+    { 1280,  576 },
+    { 1200,  540 },
+    {  960,  432 },
+    {  800,  360 },
 };
 
 /* Build an array with RRModes the first mode is the actual output mode, the
